**About Elpida Residential Programs**

Elpida Residential Programs is a non-profit supported independent-living program in San Rafael and Novato. We provide housing and supportive services to adults with serious mental illness.

We believe that with proper support, persons with mental illness can lead rich, meaningful lives within their community. The mission of Elpida Residential Programs is to assist individuals in developing the skills and support systems necessary to enable them to become more self-sufficient and lead more fulfilling lives. Above all, we aspire to instill hope, knowing that persons with mental illness can become fully functioning members of the community.

**Job Summary:**

We are seeking a Case Manager to provide care for our residents and homes. We are looking for clinically-savvy individuals, who enjoy the domestic aspects of making a house feel like a home.

The Case Manager will be responsible for providing compassionate and attentive care assuring the safety and well-being of our residents and homes. The role requires empathy and patience, as well as the ability to give firm direction and encouragement. Attention to professional boundaries is essential. The Case Manager is responsible for assessing and supporting the resident through treatment and skill building while maintaining a safe and functioning home environment.

Our current opportunities are part-time and relief positions, with the potential to become full-time in the future. We also have opportunities for Case Manager Assistants, who would manage similar tasks to that of a Case Manager but would not carry a caseload. This would be a great opportunity for those starting out in the field, all the way up to those who are retired and would like to give back to the community.

**Duties and Responsibilities:**

* Manage a case load of up to six (6) residents;
* Meet with each resident for a weekly regularly-scheduled, goal-focused individual session;
* Maintain resident charts, including written progress notes following meetings;
* Assess residents’ physical and mental wellness, needs, preferences and abilities;
* Develop individualized treatment plans, in collaboration with residents and treatment team;
* Support residents in treatment plans on a day-to-day basis within the homes and community;
* Document and evaluate resident’s progress and make adjustments as needed;
* Coordinate and maintain good relationships with providers, families, and community agencies through good communication and collaboration;
* Support and monitor medication compliance;
* Assist residents with independent living skills, including cooking, housekeeping, hygiene, money management, and transportation;
* Assist residents in scheduling and following through with appointments at outside agencies;
* Plan and lead program groups, activities, and outings;
* Transport residents to program activities and appointments in company vans;
* Coordinate and facilitate treatment conferences;
* Perform basic daily housekeeping and maintenance of homes, grounds, and property of the program;
* Facilitate a weekly house meeting with residents;
* Assist with preparing meals and menu planning;
* Ensure the safety, cleanliness, and functioning of the home;
* Use appropriate services and protocol to manage crises and ensure the safety of residents, staff, and homes;
* Perform regular safety drills for emergency preparedness;
* Support residents in maintaining a clean and safe home in a shared living environment; this can include coaching residents on housekeeping, safety protocols, communication skills and navigating challenges;
* Coordinate outside maintenance and other professional services, as needed;
* Attend weekly staff meetings and individual supervision;
* Collaborate with other professionals who provide services to Elpida residents; and
* Provide medication observation and staff coverage at other homes, as needed.

**Qualifications and Requirements:**

* Bachelor’s degree in Social Work, Psychology, Counseling, or related field, preferred;
* Experience working in a mental health, residential treatment or case management field, required;
* CPR/First Aid certification;
* Valid Driver’s License, with clean driving record;
* Must maintain personal auto insurance;
* Adept at providing person-centered care and individualized treatment;
* Must exhibit a high level of confidentiality;
* Ability to remain calm during intense situations;
* Strong capacity to take initiative and be flexible;
* Aptitude for resourcefulness and creative problem solving;
* Ability to work both independently and collaboratively and exercise good judgment;
* Excellent written and oral communication skills;
* Highly attentive to detail;
* Strong organizational and time-management skills, and ability to meet tight deadlines;
* Team player;
* Comfortability using computer systems such as Google Workspace, MS Office, and Video Conferencing; and
* Working knowledge of all standard office equipment.

Job Types: Full-time, Part-time

Pay: $25.00 - $30.00 per hour

Benefits:

* Dental insurance
* Health insurance
* Mileage reimbursement
* Paid time off
* Retirement plan
* Vision insurance

Shift availability:

* Day Shift (Preferred)
* Night Shift (Preferred)

Ability to Commute:

* San Rafael, CA 94903 (Required)

Ability to Relocate:

* San Rafael, CA 94903: Relocate before starting work (Required)

Work Location: In person

Program Manager:

Salary Range: $130K to $170K

Must have Advanced degree (minimum, master’s degree) in a relevant field from an accredited university.

Contingent offer based on contract award.

Must have at least 8+ years of experience in a leadership position directing projects teams to ensure that project management, quality management, performance, risk/issue management are integrated within the program and closely followed. Must have provable scenarios of the above experience areas in subject resume.

Experience working in Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) is preferred.

Must have or be able to obtain Tier 1 level DHS Background investigation.

Remote work will be authorized.

Must have FOIA work experience with provable scenarios in subject resumes in the following areas and perform these tasks with your hired team:

· FOIA case processing (e.g., routine, backlogged, appeal, and litigation cases);

· FOIA process and system improvements;

· FOIA systems and tools;

· FOIA reporting and shared IT work environments;

· FOIA technical knowledge.

Must have FOIA program management administration experience with provable scenarios in subject resume in the following areas and perform these tasks with your hired team:

· Kick-Off meeting;

· Non-Disclosure agreements;

· Registering employees into government access system;

· Program Management Plan development and delivery;

· Performing weekly and monthly program reporting;

· Performing monthly financial reports;

· Performing project status meetings;

· Performing ad-hoc meetings;

· Performing annual summary reports.

Pay: $130,000.00 - $170,000.00 per year

Application Question(s):

* Must have or be able to obtain Tier 1 level DHS Background investigation.

Work Location: Remote

